   120	### 3.1 Seam: shared extraction core **(owner)**
   121	
   122	One Python package, `chat-extraction-core`, owns the parsers and the canonical schema. ChatX and dNh_CRM both depend on it. Alternatives rejected:
   123	- **ChatX as sole extractor feeding dNh:** dNh needs imports it can run itself.
   124	- **Schema-only alignment:** keeps two copies of every parser.
   125	- **ChatX consuming dNh's event store:** loses reactions, backups, Instagram and PDF.
   126	
   127	### 3.2 Layout: dedicated workspace directory **(owner)**, new repository **(owner, item 1)**
   128	
   129	```
   130	~/code/chatstack/                     # new git repo, uv workspace root
   131	  pyproject.toml                      # [tool.uv.workspace] members = ["packages/*", "apps/*"]
   132	  uv.lock
   133	  packages/chat-extraction-core/      # the shared core (G1), MIT
   134	  apps/chatx/                         # the ChatX application
   135	~/code/dNh_CRM/                       # stays where it is
   136	  pyproject.toml                      # release: chat-extraction-core pinned to a tagged wheel by version and sha256
   137	~/code/Dopemux-ChatRipperXXX/         # archived: tagged, read-only reference
   138	```
   139	
   140	- **No workspace root at `~/code`.** It was verified absent; a root there would sit above every repo the owner has.
   141	- **New repo, not a history carry.** The owner confirmed this on 2026-10-21. The keep-list (§8) is ported file by file, each with a `Ported from Dopemux-ChatRipperXXX@<sha>` header. History stays in the old repo under the tag `pre-rearchitecture-2026-10-20`.
   142	- **How dNh consumes the core** *(rev 2: opus F-10, codex F21, chatgpt F29, E8)*:
   143	  - **Release builds** depend on a **built wheel pinned by version and sha256**. "dNh pins the version" means bytes, not a string.
   144	  - **Release contract:** core releases are git tags `core-vX.Y.Z`. The wheel and its sha256 are built in CI from a clean tree, and dNh's lock records that hash. Before tagging, the core's CI runs dNh's adapter tests against the new wheel.
   145	  - **Development branches** may use either form; uv documents both (E8):
   146	    - `{ path = "../chatstack/packages/chat-extraction-core", editable = true }` is a plain path dependency. It does not apply the other workspace's lock or sources.
   147	    - `{ workspace = "../chatstack" }` resolves the member by name.
   148	  - P0 proves both forms from clean clones.
   149	- **Licence and ownership** *(owner item 13)*: the core is MIT-licensed, like ChatX, and owned by the owner (DDD-Enterprises). Proprietary dNh may depend on it. Third-party notices ship with both packages.
   150	- **dNh changes** go through dNh's own governance (its `AGENTS.md` and task packets). This program demonstrates them on a dNh branch; merging is dNh's decision.
   151	
   152	### 3.3 Toolchain
   153	
   154	- **Python and SQLite.** Python `>=3.12`, dNh's floor. The interpreter is chosen by the **SQLite library it links** *(rev 2: codex F28, chatgpt F37, E4)*:
   155	  - **Why:** sqlite.org documents a WAL-reset bug. It can corrupt a WAL database when two connections write or checkpoint at the same moment. It affects 3.7.0 through 3.51.2 and is fixed in 3.51.3.
   156	  - **Floor:** the runtime must link SQLite ≥ 3.51.3, or a 3.50.x ≥ 3.50.7, or a 3.44.x ≥ 3.44.6 (the backports).
   157	  - **Enforcement:** every run records `sqlite3.sqlite_version`. A runtime below the floor refuses to open a case with `E_SQLITE_TOO_OLD`.
   158	  - **Measured 2026-10-21:** the old ChatX and dNh venvs link 3.47.1, which is below the floor. mise's Python 3.12.13 links 3.53.1.
   159	- **Tools:** `uv` (0.12.11 present), hatchling, `ruff`, `mypy --strict` for the core and a strict configuration for the app, `pytest` + `pytest-cov`, `pre-commit`, and `uv lock --check` in CI.
   160	- **The core's dependencies are listed:** `pydantic>=2,<3` and `phonenumbers>=8,<9`, nothing else *(rev 2: grok F18, codex F22)*. The core has **no network, no LLM and no storage dependencies**. Two tests enforce this: an import-graph test asserts it, and a socket guard fails any core test that opens a socket.
   161	- **App dependency bounds** are lower and upper (`>=x,<next-major`). dNh never installs the app, so these cannot conflict with dNh's pins.
   162	- **Package data** is loaded through `importlib.resources`; there is no `Path(__file__).parents[n]`. A missing schema resource is an error (`E_SCHEMA_MISSING`), never a skip (chatgpt F30).
   163	- **Model artifacts** (NER, embedding and judge models) are pinned by repository, revision and file sha256, alongside the dependency hashes, and provisioned ahead of time. Runs set `HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1` (chatgpt F36, opus F-11).
   164	- **`docs/reference/conformance.md`** *(chatgpt F38)* lists each external component with the version tested, the date and the evidence (a link or a test). The components are SQLite, sqlite-vec, Presidio, the NER models, the local model server, the Anthropic API and model ids, and uv. `chatx providers check` and P0 CI write what they observe; anything not observed stays UNKNOWN.
   165	
   166	### 3.4 Canonical message contract v2
   167	
   168	**Source of truth.** The Pydantic model in the core is the single source of truth. The JSON Schema is **generated** from it and committed (`schemas/chat.message.v2.schema.json`), and a test fails if the two drift. The version string is `chat.message.v2-draft` until the P0.5 real-database probe has run (§6). It is frozen as `chat.message.v2` after that, not before *(rev 2: grok F10)*.
   169	
   170	**Rules.** From the dNh side: `extra="forbid"`, frozen models, and timezone-aware UTC `sent_at`, with how the zone was obtained recorded (`time_source`). From the ChatX side: reactions, replies, inline attachments, outbound messages and source path provenance.
   171	
   172	**Canonical form and hashes** *(rev 2: codex F02, grok F13, agy F-02, opus F-01)*.
   173	- **Canonical JSON:** UTF-8, NFC-normalized strings, keys sorted, no insignificant whitespace, and no floats in hashed fields. This is RFC 8785 (JCS) semantics. dNh's `canonical_json` helper is checked against JCS or replaced by a JCS library (RT-2).
   174	- **`content_hash`** is a sha256 over the **immutable message core**: `platform, conv_id, msg_id, direction, sent_at, sender.handle, text, text_source, content_kind, reply_to_msg_id, thread_originator_id`, and the sorted `attachments[].sha256`.
   175	- **Never in `content_hash`:** `sender.pseudonym`, `reactions`, `edit`, `attachments[].missing/missing_reason/storage_ref/source_path`, `source_meta` and `provenance`. They arrive later or describe where the message was seen.
   176	- **`record_hash`** is a sha256 over the whole canonical record except `provenance`. It changes when anything about the message changes, including late reactions or edits.
   177	- **Why `provenance` is excluded** *(decided)*: `provenance` holds `extracted_at`, and re-importing must not change `record_hash`.
   178	
   179	**Five things v1 ran together** *(chatgpt F06)*:
   180	1. **Message identity**: `msg_id`.
   181	2. **Source observation**: `message_observations(msg_id, source_id, source_row, record_hash)`. One message seen in two overlapping exports is one message row with two observations.
   182	3. **Revision**: `record_hash`.
   183	4. **Content**: `content_hash`.
   184	5. **Raw evidence integrity**: the acquired file's sha256 in `sources` (§3.5).
   185	
   186	**Id stability contract** *(chatgpt F06, opus F-13; the `msg_id` formula was confirmed by the owner on 2026-10-21)*.
   187	- **Native ids:** the platform id where one exists (iMessage `guid`).
   188	- **Derived ids:** `sha256(platform, conv_id, sent_at, sender.handle, text, occurrence)[:32]`. `occurrence` counts earlier messages in the same source with the same `(platform, conv_id, sent_at, sender.handle, text)`, in source order, starting at 0. Identical messages sent in the same minute no longer collide.
   189	- **What is guaranteed:**
   190	  - Re-importing the same source reproduces every id.
   191	  - A later, longer export of the same chat keeps the ids of the messages it shares with the earlier one. The documented limit: messages in the same minute deleted between the two exports. The test uses two overlapping WhatsApp exports.
   192	  - The row index is stored as `provenance.source_row`, where the message was seen. It is never part of the identity.
   193	- **When a later schema version changes an id formula,** `msg_id_aliases(old_id, new_id, schema_version)` keeps old citations resolvable. Ids are never rewritten in place.
   194	- **Declined (decided):** a source-file fingerprint inside `msg_id` (opus F-13's suggestion). It would change every id on re-export.
   195	
   196	**Fields**
   197	
   198	| Field | Type | Notes |
   199	|---|---|---|
   200	| `schema_version` | `Literal["chat.message.v2-draft"]`, then `"chat.message.v2"` | frozen after the P0.5 probe |
   201	| `msg_id` | str | per the id stability contract above |
   202	| `msg_id_kind` | enum `native, derived` | |
   203	| `conv_id` | str | platform thread id (`chat_guid`) or derived per source; multi-chat rule below |
