   683	
   684	- **Error codes defined by this design:**
   685	  - `E_DB_LOCKED`, `E_DB_ACCESS_DENIED`, `E_SQLITE_TOO_OLD`, `E_CASE_LOCKED`;
   686	  - `E_TZ_REQUIRED`, `E_SCHEMA_MISSING`;
   687	  - `E_PROVIDER_NOT_LOCAL`, `E_GATE_MISMATCH`, `E_VENDOR_TERMS`, `E_VISIBILITY_LEAK`, `E_SHIELD_NOT_QUALIFIED`.
   688	  - `E_HARDFAIL_CLASS` is a per-chunk reason code in the shield report, not a run error.
   689	  - The registry generates `docs/reference/errors.md`.
   690	- **Behaviour contract** *(codex F26, chatgpt F34)*:
   691	  - **Partial or interrupted runs:** each command states what one leaves behind (a watermark, `status=partial`) and how `case resume` continues it.
   692	  - **`delete-source`** removes the source, its messages and everything derived from them by cascade *(decided, builder check)*. It also:
   693	    - drops cache entries no longer referenced, and the source's `msg_id_aliases`;
   694	    - runs `VACUUM` and a WAL checkpoint with truncation, so no content stays in free pages (`secure_delete` is on, §3.5).
   695	    It keeps the `runs` audit rows, which hold counts, not content.
   696	  - **Bundles already exported** live outside the case and are not recalled. The case records each export path, and `case purge` lists them so the owner can delete them.
   697	  - **`case purge`** removes the case directory, including `secrets/`. It keeps one audit line outside the case.
   698	  - **Dispositions:** every input record ends in exactly one disposition — imported, continuation of the previous message, system event, skipped with a reason, or quarantined with a reason. The report's counts are asserted to sum to the input count.
   699	  - **Portability:** a case directory is self-contained, with paths stored relative to the case root, so it can be moved.
   700	- **MCP** *(opus F-06, grok F7)*:
   701	  - **Redacted views only.** `chatx mcp serve` returns redacted views with surrogates for people only (§3.7, §3.8), because the MCP client's model is usually cloud-hosted.
   702	  - **`--expose-raw`** counts as cloud egress of raw text. It needs a per-session confirmation, and `runs` records it.
   703	- **Not carried from v1:** the `extract`, `analyze` and `pipeline` stubs; the Typer group registered after `__main__`; the `--config` flag that was accepted and ignored. The full disposition is in §8.
   704	
   705	### 3.13 Observability and security
   706	
   707	- **Logs.** `structlog` JSONL per run, with run ids everywhere and provider identity per call. Diagnostics use an **allowlist of fields** — ids, counts, codes, hashes. Anything else, including message text, handles and contact names, is dropped (chatgpt F31).
   708	- **Secrets** come only from environment variables named in config.
   709	- **Offline by default.** Models are provisioned ahead of time and `HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1` is set. The no-socket test covers the core, and also the app's import, identity and shield stages (opus F-11). The only outbound paths are the local provider and the explicitly configured, gated cloud provider.
   710	- **SQLite version.** Every run records `sqlite_version` (§3.3).
   711	- **Acquisition** is specified in §3.5.
   712	- **Encrypted iPhone backups** are **out of scope until P6**. `--backup-password` is removed until decryption is implemented; v1 only checked that a password was given.
   713	
   714	### 3.14 Retired outright
   715	
   716	- **Stores:** the Chroma store, the Neo4j store, and `multi_vector_store.py`. The latter is reachable today through `index --store multi` and `--multi-vector` (Appendix A.1); it is retired, not merely dead.
   717	- **Unused code:** `embeddings/*` (benchmark and psychology providers), `privacy/differential_privacy.py`, `enrichment/image_enricher.py` (placeholders), `constrained_dynamic_loader.py` (MCP tooling, not product), `enrichment/ollama_client.py` (replaced by providers), the `cli/main.py` command bodies, and `utils/config.py` (Neo4j presets, default password).
   718	- **Retired behaviours:**
   719	  - the sequential `chat.db`/`-wal`/`-shm` copy with `immutable=1`;
   720	  - the plistlib/UTF-8 heuristic in `body_normalize.py`, and the `[ATTRIBUTED_BODY_CONTENT]` placeholder;
   721	  - the `datetime.now()` fallbacks;
   722	  - the 3000–3999 "custom" reaction mapping;
   723	  - the `OR m.is_from_me = 1` contact filter;
   724	  - the `HardFailDetector` regexes;
   725	  - the hash-based `ConsistentTokenizer` tokens;
   726	  - the run-dependent chunk ids;
   727	  - the `categories` taxonomy loader.
   728	- **Tests and CI:** the old bplist fixtures, at the end of P1. `config/arch-gates.yml` and `.github/workflows/*` are rewritten in P0, not carried.
   729	- **Docs:** the entire `docs/` tree as specification. It is archived in the old repo, and the relevant intent is captured here.
   730	
   731	### 3.15 Threat model *(new in rev 2: codex F24, opus F-11, F-26, chatgpt F23, F31)*
   732	
   733	**Assets.** Raw messages and attachments; the pseudonym map and salt; the cloud API key; export bundles.
   734	
   735	**Adversaries considered:**
   736	- another local user or process;
   737	- a lost or stolen laptop;
   738	- a malicious export, ZIP, PDF or `.eml`;
   739	- a malicious or cloud-backed MCP client;
   740	- prompt injection through message content;
   741	- a misconfigured provider URL;
   742	- sync and backup services copying case data off the machine.
   743	
   744	**Out of scope.** Root on the machine, memory forensics, a compromised OS.
   745	
   746	**Controls:**
   747	- **File system.** Case directories are 0700 and files 0600. Nothing is written to `/tmp`. FileVault is required (§3.5), and per-case encryption is opt-in.
   748	- **Input limits** cover ZIP bytes, entries and compression ratio, PDF pages and database size. SQL is parameterized only, and there is no `pickle` or `eval`.
   749	- **Model output** is schema-validated. An adversarial test set of chunks containing instructions, fake JSON and fake surrogate tokens must produce the same labels as the clean-text baseline.
   750	- **Egress.** Provider locality is computed (§3.6), MCP serves redacted views only, and the gate token binds the exact request (§3.7).
   751	
   752	**Where message content can land, and the rule for each place:**
   753	
   754	| Place | Rule |
   755	|---|---|
   756	| `case.sqlite3` and its WAL, FTS shadow tables | inside the 0700 case root; deleted by `case purge` |
   757	| `secrets/` | 0700/0600; excluded from bundles by default |
   758	| `attachments/`, `sources/` | inside the case root; bytes exact |
   759	| case `tmp/`, `attachments/.tmp/` | inside the case root; swept at start; reported by `case verify` |
   760	| quarantine records | stored in the case, never in loose files |
   761	| logs | field allowlist only (ids, counts, codes, hashes) |
   762	| crash output | `pretty_exceptions_show_locals=False`; no locals printed |
   763	| model caches | pinned artifacts only; no message content written to them |
   764	| exports | §3.10 rules; secrets and analysis opt-in; content involving minors never |
   765	| dNh adapter JSONL (`--emit-jsonl`) | written into the case `tmp/`, deleted after the adapter run |
   766	| shell history | contacts may be given via `--contact-file` or a prompt |
   767	| Spotlight, iCloud, Time Machine | `.noindex` root, iCloud-synced roots refused, Time Machine exclusion offered |
   768	
   769	---
   770	
   771	## 4. Target architecture
   772	
   773	```
   774	packages/chat-extraction-core/src/chat_extraction_core/
   775	  schema/       canonical message v2 models, generated JSON Schema, canonical JSON + content/record hashes, version registry
   776	  time/         Apple-epoch converter (2001–2100 bounds), export-time grammars, --assume-tz handling
   777	  sources/
   778	    imessage/   acquisition via the backup API, schema probe + column manifest, reader,
   779	                reaction / reply / edit / system-event folds, multi-chat rule,
   780	                attributedbody/ (dNh's bounded decoder first, generic typedstream walker second),
   781	                attachment resolver (expanduser, resolve, containment)
   782	    backup/     iPhone Manifest.db acquisition and fileID resolution (unencrypted until P6)
   783	    instagram/  ZIP reader (zip-slip guard, byte/entry/ratio limits), latin-1 mojibake repair
   784	    whatsapp/   Android + iOS export grammars, structural system lines, explicit date order
   785	    pdf/        text-layer transcript parser (no OCR)
   786	    email/      .eml parser (Message-ID, In-Reply-To, References, From/To/Cc/Bcc, Date)
   787	  identity/     phonenumbers-based handle normalization, HMAC pseudonyms
   788	  fixtures/     chat.db builders from per-macOS schema snapshots, export builders, golden JSONL
   789	  (no network, no LLM, no database of its own; writes only to paths the caller gives; dependencies: pydantic, phonenumbers)
   790	
   791	apps/chatx/src/chatx/
   792	  case/         store, SQL migrations, acquisition orchestration, CAS, verify / repair / resume / backup / purge
   793	  shield/       Presidio integration, recognizers, language id, surrogates + map custody, eval harness, gate + tokens
   794	  chunk/        chunker (deterministic ids)
   795	  providers/    ChatProvider, EmbeddingProvider, openai_compat, anthropic, capabilities probe, locality check
   796	  enrich/       taxonomy compiler, structured enrichment, typed outcomes, cache, calibration, hysteresis
   797	  index/        embedding spaces, vec0 tables, FTS, filter-then-KNN, RRF fusion
   798	  query/        answers with citations, citation-support check
   799	  report/       manifests, run / redaction / missing-attachment reports, export bundle + custody, import-bundle
   800	  analysis/     (phase 6) construct map, indicators
   801	  cli/          Typer app, RFC 9457 problems, exit codes
   802	  mcp/          (phase 7) redacted views
   803	```
   804	
   805	**Data flow:**
   806	
   807	`core acquire + iterate → case import (probe, map, quarantine) → identity → chunk (membership) → local pass (shield detection + local enrichment) → cloud pass (eligible chunks only, surrogate rendering, through the gate) → index → query / export`
   808	
   809	- **Within ChatX.** Every stage reads and writes the case database. There are no file hand-offs between stages, which is what broke v1.
   810	- **From the core** *(decided, builder check)*. The core yields canonical messages and disposition records (quarantined or skipped, each with a reason), so ChatX and dNh get the same accounting. `chatx import` consumes them directly.
   811	- **JSONL** is written only for `--emit-jsonl` and the dNh adapter tests (§9, chatgpt F03).
   812	
   813	**Importer fidelity** *(chatgpt F13, codex F08, grok F12, agy F-04, F-11, F-19, opus F-07, F-15, F-31)*. Each original export file is acquired into `sources/` with its sha256, like `chat.db`.
   814	
   815	| Source | Reads | Keeps raw in `source_meta` | Cannot recover | `source_locator` |
   816	|---|---|---|---|---|
   817	| iMessage `chat.db` | the §3.4 column manifest | every manifest column without a canonical field; blobs in `message_blobs` | membership history; messages Messages already purged | `ROWID` |
   818	| iPhone backup | the same, via `Manifest.db` fileIDs | the same | encrypted backups (until P6) | `ROWID` + fileID |
   819	| Instagram ZIP | messages JSON (sender, `timestamp_ms`, content, media, reactions, shares) | unknown keys verbatim | handles (display names only); edits | JSON pointer |
   820	| WhatsApp text export | Android and iOS bracketed line grammars; `--date-order dmy/mdy` explicit | the raw line and markers (`<Media omitted>`, deleted-message lines) as `source_meta.wa_marker` | time zone (`--assume-tz` required); seconds on Android; handles (display names only); reactions; replies | line number |
   821	| PDF transcript | text layer only; `platform=pdf_transcript` | the raw line | attachments; time zone (`--assume-tz` required); lines without a timestamp are quarantined | page + line |
   822	| Email `.eml` | `Message-ID, In-Reply-To, References, From, To, Cc, Bcc, Date`; `reply_to_msg_id` ← `In-Reply-To`; `conv_id` ← root of the `References` chain; direction from `--me` | all headers | a missing or `-0000` zone → `source_tz=None` and the §3.4 time rules | `Message-ID` + file |
   823	
   824	**WhatsApp rules.**
   825	- **System lines** are detected **structurally**: a line with no `Name:` prefix is a system line. Substring matching is never used, because v1 dropped ordinary messages containing words like "added" or "left".
   826	- **Continuations.** Lines before the first header and continuation lines are kept, not discarded.
   827	
   828	**Instagram rules.**
   829	- **Mojibake.** The latin-1→UTF-8 re-decode runs only when it round-trips cleanly. The golden fixture includes emoji and accented names, because mojibake names evade the PERSON recognizer.
   830	- **Email ids.** These come from the normalized `Message-ID` header, falling back to a hash of normalized headers plus body, so the same mail saved twice dedupes.
   831	
   832	---
   833	
   834	## 5. Contracts the builder must honour
   835	
   836	1. **Canonical message v2.**
   837	   - The version is `chat.message.v2-draft` until the P0.5 probe, then frozen.
   838	   - A breaking change bumps the version string, adds a migration note and records the affected ids in `msg_id_aliases`.
   839	   - dNh pins the core wheel by version and sha256.
   840	2. **Schema generation test.** The committed JSON Schema equals the generated schema. Schemas load through `importlib.resources`; a missing one is `E_SCHEMA_MISSING`.
   841	3. **Id stability.** Re-importing a source reproduces every `msg_id` and `chunk_id`. An overlapping later export keeps shared ids, within the §3.4 limit. Tests cover both.
   842	4. **Problems and exit codes.**
   843	   - Errors use one RFC 9457 shape and one code convention.
   844	   - Exit codes are 0–4 (§3.12).
   845	   - `docs/reference/errors.md` is generated from the code's error registry.
   846	5. **Gate semantics.**
   847	   - Every call to a cloud provider takes a gate token bound to the exact serialized request.
   848	   - Tests prove that a missing, forged, expired, foreign or mismatched token cannot send.
   849	   - Cloud request types have no attachment, `msg_id` or `conv_id` fields.
   850	6. **Provider identity.** Requested and observed models are recorded separately, with `call_config_hash` per call. UNKNOWN is never replaced by the requested value.
   851	7. **dNh adapter totality.** The adapter test enumerates every `(platform, direction, content_kind)` triple from the enums and asserts that exactly one disposition rule matches it (§9). A new enum value fails the test until it has a rule.
   852	8. **Coverage.**
   853	   - `--cov-fail-under=90` on lines over `chat_extraction_core` and `chatx`, with no `omit` beyond `tests/`.
   854	   - Branch coverage and a mutation-testing (`mutmut`) kill rate of at least 80 % on `shield/` and the gate. The floor is raised as it is met and never lowered *(decided, builder check)*.
   855	9. **No network.**
   856	   - The core never opens a socket.
   857	   - The app's import, identity and shield stages never open a socket.
   858	   - Model artifacts load offline.
   859	10. **SQLite floor.** A case never opens under SQLite below the floor (§3.3).
   860	
   861	---
   862	
   863	## 6. Phases and exit criteria
   864	
   865	The order follows two rules, both new in rev 2:
   866	- **Risk first** *(opus F-24)*: the P0.5 spikes test the unknowns that decide feasibility before anything is built on them.
   867	- **Each phase's exit uses only that phase's outputs** *(codex F23, chatgpt F32)*.
   868	
   869	| Phase | Scope | Exit criteria (all must be PASS) |
   870	|---|---|---|
   871	| **P0 Workspace** | `~/code/chatstack` repo; uv workspace; two empty packages; CI (ruff, mypy, pytest, `uv lock --check`, `pip-audit`) testing the **installed wheel** in a fresh venv outside the checkout; `.github/workflows/*` rewritten, `arch-gates.yml` not carried; pre-commit; ADR template; `conformance.md` skeleton; an interpreter linking SQLite at or above the floor; this document copied in | A green CI run, its URL recorded, that includes the failure-path tests (`E_GATE_MISMATCH` → exit 3 and `E_SCHEMA_MISSING` → exit 1, per §3.12, as stubs); `uv sync` works from a clean clone; a dNh dev branch resolves the core by both the `path` and `workspace` forms, and that branch's CI installs a pinned wheel and passes (merging it is dNh's decision, not a ChatX exit criterion); `sqlite_version` recorded and ≥ floor |
   872	| **P0.5 Spikes** (no shipped code) | (a) the structure-only probe on the owner's real `chat.db`: schema-probe result, typedstream decode coverage, reaction-prefix linkage, multi-chat counts, 2006/3006 codes; (b) Presidio + spaCy, GLiNER and OpenAI Privacy Filter recall on the first ~300 owner-labelled messages; (c) dNh dedupe-continuity replay on a copy of dNh's database: new, duplicate and would-correct counts; (d) the chosen local model's structured output at target throughput; (e) `vec0` scan timing at 100k and 1M synthetic chunks | Each spike's numbers recorded in `docs/measurements.md`. A result may reorder or cut later phases. The schema stays `v2-draft` until (a) has run |
   873	| **P1 Extraction core** | Schema v2 (frozen after P0.5 a); acquisition; iMessage (manifest, folds, decoders, attachments); unencrypted backups; Instagram (mojibake, limits); WhatsApp; PDF; email; identity; fixtures from schema snapshots; `chatx import imessage --probe` | Golden tests per source, with the real-shape fixtures of §7; schema drift test; WAL snapshot test; reaction-fold property test; id-stability tests; a real `chat.db` smoke run documented with counts; the dNh adapter test passes on a dNh branch with dNh's suite green; V1 resolved; old bplist fixtures and tests that pin retired behaviour deleted |
   874	| **P2 Case store, chunking, CLI skeleton** | Store, migrations, invariants, lock, CAS; `case create/status/verify/repair/resume/backup/delete-source/purge`; manifest, `runs`, metrics; FTS5 over messages; chunking (§3.8) | Import of 100k synthetic messages with throughput and RSS **recorded** in `docs/measurements.md`; `case verify` checks every §3.5 invariant and re-hashes attachments; a crash-and-resume test; deterministic chunk ids test |
   875	| **P3 Shield v2 and local provider** | Presidio integration, ported recognizers, NER engine chosen by the eval, language id, surrogates and map custody, eval harness (synthetic and real), `shield_evals`, gate and tokens, taxonomy-based hard-fail with definitions drafted for the owner; `ChatProvider` + `OpenAICompatProvider`, capability probe, locality check, second-opinion judge | Synthetic eval in CI; refusal-path tests (exit 3, `E_GATE_MISMATCH`, `E_VENDOR_TERMS`, `E_PROVIDER_NOT_LOCAL`, `E_VISIBILITY_LEAK`); token-grammar and escaping tests; mutation kill rate ≥ 80 % on shield and gate; once the owner's labels exist, the real-sample evaluation — including the second-opinion judge's recall on the same sample — is run and recorded. Passing P3 on synthetic results unlocks the **local** pipeline only. The cloud tier unlocks when the real-sample evaluation passes; that is a separate local gate, recorded and reported as such |
   876	| **P4 Enrichment and cloud provider** | `labels.yml` 1.3 and its compiler; structured enrichment with typed outcomes; cache; stateful hysteresis; calibration on the gold set; `AnthropicProvider`; the operation contract; the cloud path through the gate | Contract tests against recorded responses (no live model in CI); an owner-run live smoke of the request shape against the configured cloud model; the adversarial prompt-injection set passes; every enrichment row joins to its messages and appears in the run report |
   877	| **P5 Index, query, export** | Embedding spaces, `vec0`, filter-then-KNN, RRF, citations, `query`, citation-support check, retrieval gold set; export bundle with custody; `import-bundle` | Recall@k on the gold set recorded; retrieval latency at **1M synthetic chunks** recorded; a bundle verifies and round-trips through `import-bundle`; stale-citation detection test. If the latency target fails twice, an ADR chooses between file-based ANN candidates (usearch, hnswlib) |
   878	| **P6 Analysis lane and extras** | Construct map and indicators; image enrichment; audio transcription; encrypted backups | Each sub-feature has its own ADR, evaluation and opt-in flag; analysis labels have inter-rater agreement before shipping |
   879	| **P7 MCP and polish** | `chatx mcp serve` (redacted views; `--expose-raw` recorded as egress); generated CLI and error reference; MkDocs; old repo archived | Docs generated from code; an MCP egress test; old repo tagged, and its README points here |
   880	
   881	Each phase gets its own implementation plan (superpowers:writing-plans).
   882	
   883	---
   884	
   885	## 7. Quality gates (global)
   886	
   887	- **Static checks:** `ruff check` and `ruff format --check`; `mypy --strict` for the core and a strict configuration for the app.
   888	- **Coverage:** `pytest --cov-fail-under=90` over both whole packages with no omit list, plus branch coverage and a `mutmut` kill rate of at least 80 % on shield and gate code (opus F-22, F-35).
   889	- **Supply chain:** `uv lock --check` and `pip-audit`; dependency and model hashes pinned.
   890	- **Fixtures:**
   891	  - **Generated, not copied.** Fixture databases are generated from per-macOS-version **schema snapshots** (DDL only, captured by the probe; no rows from the owner's data), so goldens cannot pass against a schema that does not exist (opus F-21).
   892	  - **Real-shape artifacts.** Fixtures include:
   893	    - typedstream `attributedBody` blobs (dNh's observed prefixes plus sanitized probe captures);
   894	    - `p:0/` and `bp:` reaction guids;
   895	    - `thread_originator_guid`, `~/Library` paths and multi-chat joins;
   896	    - `date_edited`/`date_retracted`, group events and sticker type 1000;
   897	    - WhatsApp Android and iOS exports in at least two locales;
   898	    - Instagram with mojibake;
   899	    - `.eml` with `References`.
   900	  - **Legacy tests.** The old bplist fixtures, and tests that pin retired behaviour, are deleted at the end of P1 (grok F17).
   901	  - **Decoder test.** dNh's `test_decodes_four_byte_little_endian_length` actually encodes its `0x8000` length in the two-byte form. The ported test is fixed to exercise the four-byte form (chatgpt F09).
   902	- **Property tests:**
   903	  - the Apple-epoch converter (bounds 2001–2100, `0` → `None`);
   904	  - handle normalization;
   905	  - reaction and edit fold algebra (any interleaving of adds and removes reaches the same state and history);
   906	  - the WhatsApp grammars;
   907	  - id stability across overlapping exports.
   908	- **Security tests:**
   909	  - the no-socket core and offline app stages;
   910	  - a cloud send without a valid token fails;
   911	  - modes on the salt and secrets;
   912	  - no attachment or id field on cloud request models;
   913	  - token escaping;
   914	  - the adversarial injection set;
   915	  - a log-allowlist test, which greps a fixture run's logs for fixture text.
   916	- **Performance.** Numbers are measurements, not promises. `pytest -m perf` (opt-in) records throughput, latency and RSS into `docs/measurements.md`, with the machine and commit.
   917	  - The old targets become tracked measurements, promoted to gates only once met twice: ≥10k msg/min ingest, p95 ≤150 ms retrieval, <4 GB for 1M messages, and a cache hit rate ≥80 %.
   918	  - P5 measures at 1M chunks.
   919	- **CI vs local.** CI shows the synthetic shield evaluation only. The real-sample evaluation uses the owner's data, so it is a separate local gate, recorded per run. The docs say so (chatgpt F33).
   920	
   921	---
