/Users/hue/code/Dopemux-ChatRipperXXX/docs/superpowers/audits/2026-10-20-design-audit/out/design-revision-plan.md:13:Problem: the design keeps `imessage/db.py` and calls it "WAL-safe". The code copies `chat.db`, `-wal`, `-shm` sequentially with `shutil.copy2` (not a snapshot) and then opens the copy with `immutable=1`, which makes SQLite ignore the copied WAL — recent messages are silently dropped. The copy lives in a `TemporaryDirectory` under `/tmp`.
/Users/hue/code/Dopemux-ChatRipperXXX/docs/superpowers/audits/2026-10-20-design-audit/out/design-revision-plan.md:16:- Acquire with the **SQLite online backup API** (`sqlite3.Connection.backup`, stdlib) from a `mode=ro` connection on the live db into `cases/<case>/sources/<source-id>/chat.sqlite3`. The backup API produces a self-contained database (WAL contents included), so the snapshot is opened `mode=ro` without `immutable=1`.
/Users/hue/code/Dopemux-ChatRipperXXX/docs/superpowers/audits/2026-10-20-design-audit/out/design-revision-plan.md:20:- **SQLite floor** *(decided 2026-10-21; was RT-1)*: sqlite.org documents a WAL-reset bug that can corrupt a WAL database when two connections write or checkpoint at the same moment. It is present in 3.7.0 through 3.51.2 and fixed in 3.51.3 (2026-03-13), with backports in 3.44.6 and 3.50.7 (**E4**; the supervisor re-read sqlite.org/wal.html). The runtime must link SQLite ≥ 3.51.3, or a 3.50.x ≥ 3.50.7, or a 3.44.x ≥ 3.44.6. Every run records `sqlite3.sqlite_version`. On this Mac (2026-10-21) the ChatX and dNh venvs link 3.47.1, which is below the floor, and mise's Python 3.12.13 links 3.53.1. So the new repo's interpreter is chosen by the SQLite it links, and P0 checks it.
/Users/hue/code/Dopemux-ChatRipperXXX/docs/superpowers/audits/2026-10-20-design-audit/out/design-revision-plan.md:23:- *(chatgpt F37)* Same question as the SQLite floor above, now answered. Added: P0 records the SQLite library ChatX actually links (`sqlite3.sqlite_version`, not the Python version) on the owner's machine and in CI. The floor is written into §3.5 with T12's concurrency rules, and a runtime below it refuses to open a case (`E_SQLITE_TOO_OLD`).
/Users/hue/code/Dopemux-ChatRipperXXX/docs/superpowers/audits/2026-10-20-design-audit/out/design-revision-plan.md:78:- *(chatgpt F14)* Wiring the decoder does not fix history. Backfill is a separate one-time migration: the adapter replays the whole snapshot, not only dNh's bounded lookback window, and rows dNh already holds dedupe as before (`UNIQUE(dedupe_scope, dedupe_hash)`). Rows dNh stored with no text that now decode cannot be corrected by re-sending, because the dedupe key is unchanged and dNh's log is append-only; the owner chose to leave them and count them (item 12, 2026-10-21): the adapter reports how many stored events lack text that now decodes, and no correction event type is added. The P0.5 replay spike (T19 c) reports new, duplicate and would-correct counts before anything is sent.
