/Users/hue/code/Dopemux-ChatRipperXXX/docs/superpowers/audits/2026-10-20-design-audit/out/design-revision-plan.md:134:- *(chatgpt F05)* Covered by the eligibility and statistics bullets above. Added: required classes come from the taxonomy (opus F-04), and required **languages** are declared per case by the owner. Recall is reported per class and language; a chunk whose detected language is not declared is `cloud_eligible=false` (local language identification, **RT-16**). A missing real-sample evaluation keeps the cloud tier off; P3 can exit on synthetic results for the local pipeline only (T19).
/Users/hue/code/Dopemux-ChatRipperXXX/docs/superpowers/audits/2026-10-20-design-audit/out/design-revision-plan.md:169:- *(chatgpt F24)* Invariants `case verify` checks: every message has at least one observation (T02); every chunk's `msg_ids` exist with a matching `record_hash`; FTS row count equals message count; each embedding space has one vector per chunk (T13). A source stays `status=partial` until its last import batch commits, then becomes `complete`. Messages, sources and attachments are the evidence; chunks, FTS, embeddings and enrichments are derived and disposable, and `case repair` rebuilds them from the evidence tables. `chatx case backup` uses the SQLite backup API (T01).
