| AST-F25 | HIGH | CONFIRMED | packet:L118–120 | [S1,S6] The dNh handoff does not specify the transition from editable source experiments to a wheel-locked branch. | dnh:pyproject.toml:L11–25 has no core requirement/source table; dnh:.github/workflows/ci.yml:L13–23 checks out only dNh before syncing. | Give dNh's authorized owner exact manifest surfaces, separate path/workspace experiments, and a final wheel-source/lock transition with no remaining sibling override and installed-origin evidence. |
| AST-F26 | HIGH | CONFIRMED | packet:L270–272 | [S6,S10,S13] The proposed private release is not reachable by dNh's workflow token by default, and no alternative is authorized. | dNh CI contains no cross-repository credential/download step; [GITHUB_TOKEN is scoped to its workflow repository](https://docs.github.com/en/actions/concepts/security/github_token). | Resolve private-asset access under separate dNh authority using a scoped credential or approved artifact delivery route, document URL/download and digest verification, and keep credentials out of manifests and logs. |
| AST-F27 | HIGH | CONFIRMED | packet:L81 | [S6,S9] A green existing dNh workflow does not by itself prove a frozen, hashed wheel installation. | dnh:.github/workflows/ci.yml:L3–6 requires main push or a PR; L17 leaves uv unversioned and L23 syncs without --locked; X4 specifies neither an authorized trigger nor a concrete hash-enforcing install. | Define the authorized PR/trigger, consumer uv pin, immutable dNh lock and wheel URL/hash representation, and ensure subsequent sync/run steps preserve the verified artifact. |
| AST-F28 | HIGH | CONFIRMED | packet:L117 | [S6,S10] The clean-clone instruction names the existing primary repository paths. | It calls for clean clones at ~/code/dNh_CRM and ~/code/chatstack, although dNh exists and Task 1 will have created chatstack. | Use a unique authorized scratch parent with sibling dNh_CRM/chatstack clones at recorded SHAs, preserve primary checkouts, and remove only task-owned scratch artifacts under their governing authority. |
