| AST-F38 | INFO | CONFIRMED | packet:L257 | [S5,S13,S15] Release hashes are not independent provenance; current immutability/attestation options deserve an explicit P0 decision. | [GitHub immutable releases](https://docs.github.com/en/code-security/concepts/supply-chain-security/immutable-releases) protect tags/assets and produce release attestations; [artifact attestations](https://docs.github.com/en/enterprise-cloud%40latest/actions/concepts/security/artifact-attestations) can include SBOMs; account eligibility is UNKNOWN. | Record whether immutable draft-then-publish releases, build provenance and SBOMs are enabled or deferred, verifying account support and permissions without widening P0 into a publishing-platform project. |
| AST-F39 | INFO | CONFIRMED | packet:L161 | [S2,S15] Dependency groups and an alpha release are sound choices; neither requires switching to PyPI. | [PEP 735](https://peps.python.org/pep-0735/) keeps dev groups out of wheel metadata; [pip](https://pip.pypa.io/en/stable/cli/pip_install/) and [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/concepts/resolution/) document pre-release selection; [Trusted Publishing](https://docs.pypi.org/trusted-publishers/) concerns index publication. | Retain the dev group and exact 0.0.1a0 wheel pin, verify resolver policy with the chosen uv/pip versions, and leave PyPI Trusted Publishing out unless a later index release is authorized. |
| AST-F40 | INFO | CONFIRMED | packet:L313 | [S1,S6,S15] The external-workspace source form is documented and should not be rejected merely because dNh is outside chatstack. | Current [uv workspace documentation](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/concepts/projects/workspaces/) supports workspace as a root-path string; dNh's >=3.12 and pydantic 2.12.5 are textually compatible with the proposed core bounds. | Retain both X3 experiments under dNh authority, record the actual consumer uv version and each lock/origin result, and keep documentation support separate from a NOT_RUN resolver qualification. |

## Decision challenges

- **DECISION CHALLENGE — decision 5, downstream exit exclusion (AST-F02).** The latest owner instruction excludes X3/X4 from ChatX exit criteria, so this audit honors that boundary. However, the frozen spec still requires their PASS. Approving local P0 without a separately named downstream status risks representing installation compatibility as proven; retaining them as implicit blockers would make ChatX wait on authority it does not hold. Settle this with an owner-recorded canonical amendment defining local P0 completion and downstream integration pending, with X3/X4 remaining NOT_RUN until evidenced.
- **DECISION CHALLENGE — proposed B14 private distribution, not an already-decided visibility change (AST-F26).** Private GitHub assets require a consumer access route beyond assuming dNh's repository token can read chatstack. Keeping privacy without that route leaves X4 unusable; making the repository public merely to avoid authentication would expose material without authority. Settle this with the owner's visibility decision and a separately authorized dNh download/credential or artifact-delivery design; do not silently change visibility.

## Unverified impressions

None. Runtime availability, actual build/test outcomes and account-specific permissions remain unverified as detailed in Output B; no missing-runtime evidence has been promoted to PASS.


