| AST-F21 | HIGH | CONFIRMED | packet:L257–258 | [S5,S10] A matching tag immediately enables publication without an enforced green-CI dependency. | Task 7 L276 manually waits for green, but release.yml has no check of required jobs on the tagged commit and runs independently of ci.yml. | Make publication fail closed until all required checks for the dereferenced tag commit succeed, and retain the owner-only tag authority. |
| AST-F22 | BLOCKER | CONFIRMED | packet:L276 | [S5,S9] The packet permits publishing bytes that have never passed the installed-wheel tests. | The release rebuild is not tested; a mismatch with wheel-tests is explicitly nonfatal, and X3/X4 may remain NOT_RUN. | Keep G-E's tagged-tree rebuild but run the required installed-wheel checks on that exact release artifact before upload, recording its tested digest even when reproducibility remains non-gating. |
| AST-F23 | HIGH | CONFIRMED | packet:L257 | [S2,S5] The broad core-v* trigger has no tag-to-package identity validation. | The command builds whatever metadata the tagged tree contains and labels the release with GITHUB_REF_NAME; a tag name alone cannot establish version agreement. | Reject malformed or mismatched tags, require the approved P0 tag and notes file, assert a clean checkout and one expected core wheel, and compare tag suffix with wheel metadata before publishing. |
