| AST-F37 | MEDIUM | CONFIRMED | packet:L245–261 | [S4,S7,S13] Runner qualification and CI operational controls remain incomplete. | macOS arm64 is required but not asserted at runtime; no job timeout, uv version setup, cache policy or unique matrix-artifact naming is specified, and actionlint is optional. | Specify the approved runner/uv/Python setup, assert arm64 and the SQLite floor in the test interpreter, set finite timeouts and isolated artifact names, and either disable caches or key them by platform/tool/lock inputs. |
| AST-F38 | INFO | CONFIRMED | packet:L257 | [S5,S13,S15] Release hashes are not independent provenance; current immutability/attestation options deserve an explicit P0 decision. | [GitHub immutable releases](https://docs.github.com/en/code-security/concepts/supply-chain-security/immutable-releases) protect tags/assets and produce release attestations; [artifact attestations](https://docs.github.com/en/enterprise-cloud%40latest/actions/concepts/security/artifact-attestations) can include SBOMs; account eligibility is UNKNOWN. | Record whether immutable draft-then-publish releases, build provenance and SBOMs are enabled or deferred, verifying account support and permissions without widening P0 into a publishing-platform project. |
| AST-F39 | INFO | CONFIRMED | packet:L161 | [S2,S15] Dependency groups and an alpha release are sound choices; neither requires switching to PyPI. | [PEP 735](https://peps.python.org/pep-0735/) keeps dev groups out of wheel metadata; [pip](https://pip.pypa.io/en/stable/cli/pip_install/) and [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/concepts/resolution/) document pre-release selection; [Trusted Publishing](https://docs.pypi.org/trusted-publishers/) concerns index publication. | Retain the dev group and exact 0.0.1a0 wheel pin, verify resolver policy with the chosen uv/pip versions, and leave PyPI Trusted Publishing out unless a later index release is authorized. |
