## What I could not check

All implementation tests, installs, uv sync/lock/build operations, remote creation, workflow runs, release uploads and dNh branch changes are **NOT_RUN**, as required by this read-only audit. Blocking rows ask the owner to resolve the packet's instructions before approval; they do not authorize those operations now. AST-C31–C34 apply before separately authorized dNh work and do not block ChatX's local exit.

**PASS — input binding and read-only observations:** all three snapshot hashes equal their cc18536 git blobs; the design hash equals the brief. The next-steps snapshot hash is f5b20b0a711c1b27b86fbfe3f6275ad32cec1584ad4b461b28c19a607559baaa. Local uv reports 0.12.11 (4b53f66b7, 2026-09-08, aarch64-apple-darwin); the allowed bare-python SQLite query reports 3.53.1. That SQLite observation is not proof about a future chatstack venv, dNh venv or CI interpreter. Supervisor reads confirmed the decisive dNh metadata/workflow facts; the delegated reviewer also compared the supplied digest against direct packaging files.

**FAIL — packet fitness:** the two BLOCKER findings and the HIGH/MEDIUM findings are unresolved. **UNKNOWN:** selected future runner images, their SQLite builds, exact installed tool behaviors, private-repository access, action policy, attestation availability, vulnerability-service outcomes, cost and served subagent identity. Current documentation supports external-workspace syntax and prerelease handling; selected-version resolver behavior is still NOT_RUN. The dNh import pipeline remains its existing normalizer/event-store/cursor flow; no adapter to the new core exists as a result of this audit, and installation alone would not validate that future integration.

Authority used: the latest access/output wrapper and complete master brief, frozen inputs, supplied/repository instructions and the independent-audit skill. The brief's Markdown formats override that skill's default JSON report. Excluded paths, secret files and owner databases were not opened. PAL-style inspect/trace/challenge/precommit reasoning was performed locally; no PAL service call is claimed.

Git state and files touched: ChatX remains at cc185366aca4b8912993b1400405c6eaebacfe6b with pre-existing unrelated dirt; the audit directory was already untracked. dNh HEAD was observed at e8bbcadb19f0f72e80f708e1c1073a3cb5aa45b1 on migrate-cheaperinference with no tracked changes reported; its untracked state was not inventoried. The only writes from this audit are report-astra.md and preapproval-astra.md in the authorized out directory; no commit, push, tag, implementation or acceptance was performed. One bounded read-only packaging subtask was delegated, with no escalation or retry.

Rollback: remove only these two new audit outputs if the owner rejects them; no repository implementation rollback is needed. Requested next step: revise and re-freeze the packet against the blocking checklist, then obtain owner approval; retain dNh checks and the P0 pre-tag adapter test as NOT_RUN until their respective scope permits evidence.

