+- **DECISION CHALLENGE — decision 5, downstream exit exclusion (AST-F02).** The latest owner instruction excludes X3/X4 from ChatX exit criteria, so this audit honors that boundary. However, the frozen spec still requires their PASS. Approving local P0 without a separately named downstream status risks representing installation compatibility as proven; retaining them as implicit blockers would make ChatX wait on authority it does not hold. Settle this with an owner-recorded canonical amendment defining local P0 completion and downstream integration pending, with X3/X4 remaining NOT_RUN until evidenced.
+- **DECISION CHALLENGE — proposed B14 private distribution, not an already-decided visibility change (AST-F26).** Private GitHub assets require a consumer access route beyond assuming dNh's repository token can read chatstack. Keeping privacy without that route leaves X4 unusable; making the repository public merely to avoid authentication would expose material without authority. Settle this with the owner's visibility decision and a separately authorized dNh download/credential or artifact-delivery design; do not silently change visibility.
